findings.body:
`handleJSONSchemaChange` ends its happy path with `return True`. `True` is not a TypeScript/JavaScript identifier (the literal is `true`). `tsc` and `next build` will fail with "Cannot find name 'True'".

Even if the type check were bypassed, the code would throw a `ReferenceError` on every valid JSON edit. The `catch` block would swallow it and return `null`. The state write happens before the throw, so the feature appears to work while hiding the error.

::diff{file="web/app/components/app/configuration/config-var/config-modal/index.tsx" lines="130-144"}

The return value is never used by `CodeEditor`, so the fix is simply to drop the return.

::suggestion{file="web/app/components/app/configuration/config-var/config-modal/index.tsx" lines="136-140"}
try {
  JSON.parse(value)
  handlePayloadChange('json_schema')(value)
}
catch {
  return null
}

`handleJSONSchemaChange` returns early on invalid JSON without updating `tempPayload`. The editor's visible text and the stored value then diverge. If the user types an invalid schema and clicks confirm, `handleConfirm` validates the previous valid value, which passes, and saves the stale schema with no error.

The new `variableConfig.errorMsg.jsonSchemaInvalid` branch in `handleConfirm` is therefore effectively unreachable from the UI. The user's edit is lost without any feedback.

The fix is to keep the raw editor text in state and validate it on confirm. Keep the pretty-printed `jsonSchemaStr` for display only when the text is valid, so it does not overwrite what the user is typing.

::code{file="web/app/components/app/configuration/config-var/config-modal/index.tsx" lines="310-323"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The `jsonSchemaStr` memo re-stringifies on each state change. If the state holds raw invalid text, the memo must return the raw text rather than `''`, or Monaco will be reset mid-edit.

`normalizedJsonSchema` is computed but never read. The save uses `payloadToSave`, which applies the empty-to-undefined rule inline, so the variable is dead code. It also fails the repository's unused-variable lint.

::diff{file="web/app/components/app/configuration/config-var/config-modal/index.tsx" lines="248-257"}

Delete the line, or use it to build `payloadToSave` so the two do not drift.
